Repair the complete CommonJS source below and return a corrected complete source file exporting exactly `{ projectFields }`.

`projectFields(source, liveKeys)` copies a plain record while selectively preserving references. `source` must be a non-null, non-array object, and `liveKeys` must be an array of unique strings naming existing own enumerable properties. Invalid shapes or missing keys throw `TypeError`; duplicate live keys throw `RangeError`.

Return a new object containing the source's own enumerable string-keyed properties in their original enumeration order. Values named by `liveKeys` must be returned by the exact same reference. Other arrays and non-null objects must be shallow-copied; other values are assigned directly. The source, `liveKeys`, and nested values must not be mutated. Empty objects and empty live-key arrays are valid.

Known-bad source:
```javascript
function projectFields(source, liveKeys) {
  if (!source || typeof source !== 'object' || Array.isArray(source)) throw new TypeError('Invalid source');
  if (!Array.isArray(liveKeys)) throw new TypeError('Live keys must be an array');
  const live = new Set();
  for (const key of liveKeys) {
    if (typeof key !== 'string' || !Object.prototype.propertyIsEnumerable.call(source, key)) {
      throw new TypeError('Invalid live key');
    }
    if (live.has(key)) throw new RangeError('Duplicate live key');
    live.add(key);
  }
  const output = {};
  for (const key of Object.keys(source)) {
    const value = source[key];
    if (Array.isArray(value)) output[key] = value.slice();
    else if (value && typeof value === 'object') output[key] = { ...value };
    else output[key] = value;
  }
  return output;
}

module.exports = { projectFields };
```

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

